        "abstract_source_sha256": "34af8011ff03036283dae6ae51b9a4ddee9410026b29e6988b00ccda2576fbf6",
        "abstract_tex": "Let $F=\\Q_3$ and let $E/F$ be its unramified quadratic extension. We give an explicit checkable argument that the Langlands quotient with segments\n$[4,6],[2,5],[3,3],[1,4],[0,2]$ is Galois invariant, is not an entire proper parabolic induction, and has no invariant linear form for any Hermitian stabilizer in $\\GL_{15}(E)$. The analytic proof assembles the period bases and functional equations of Feigon--Lapid--Offen: two invertible nested-segment swaps expose five necessary opposite-lift conditions forming an odd cycle. Noninduction follows from the Lapid--M\\'inguez ladder-side matching criterion, with all fifteen partition obstructions displayed. The total multiplicity is zero rather than the two predicted by the historical $k=1$ multiplicity conjecture. Historical priority and overlap with Luo--Zha, DOI \\href{https://doi.org/10.1007/s11464-025-0256-0}{10.1007/s11464-025-0256-0}, remain \\textbf{UNKNOWN}: their complete paper was unavailable for comparison. No firstness or worldwide novelty claim is made.",
